      "id": "overview-sticky",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        160,
        20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Day 58 Solution: OAuth vs API Keys\n\nThis demo workflow is a credential smoke test: one native node per service, each running the simplest possible authenticated call, feeding a summary of which credentials actually work.\n\n**Credentials needed to run for real:** Slack OAuth2, Notion API (internal integration token), Airtable Personal Access Token, Gmail OAuth2, OpenAI API key. None are wired in this file on purpose -- add your own under each node's Credentials field after import.\n\nSee DAILY_TASKS/DAY_58_OAuth_vs_API_Keys.md for the full task.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 440
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "oauth-vs-key-sticky",
      "name": "OAuth vs API Key Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        620,
        20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## OAuth 2.0 vs API Key\n\n**OAuth 2.0 (Gmail, Slack, Notion):** used when the workflow acts on behalf of a specific user against their own data (their inbox, their workspace, their pages). Scoped, revocable, and tied to a login/consent flow.\n\n**API Key (Airtable, OpenAI):** used for service-to-service calls where there's no per-user login screen -- a base or a model endpoint you're calling as yourself, not impersonating another account. Simpler to set up but must be stored/rotated carefully.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 380
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "manual-trigger",
      "name": "Start Credential Test",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
